### CTRS FloorPlan REST API — VS Code REST Client file
### Run `npm run seed` first so the two seeded floor plans exist.
### Click "Send Request" above each block. After each write, refresh the collection in Compass.

@host = http://localhost:5000
@seededId = 66f0000000000000000000a1

### 0. API info
GET {{host}}/

### 1. GET ALL — list every floor plan
GET {{host}}/floorplans

### 1b. GET ALL with filter — only active plans
GET {{host}}/floorplans?status=active

### 2. GET ONE — seeded "Concert Layout" plan
GET {{host}}/floorplans/{{seededId}}

### 3. POST — create a new floor plan (response is captured as "created")
### Table capacity is optional: it defaults from the type (circle 2, square 4, sofa 6, triangle 1).
### Each zone carries the venue's standard price per table type; every type used in the zone must be priced.
# @name created
POST {{host}}/floorplans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Rooftop Layout - DJ Night",
  "venue": "La Loy Bar, Nanglinchee / Rama 3",
  "extraPersonFee": 600,
  "landmarks": [
    { "name": "DJ BOOTH", "position": { "x": 50, "y": 5 } },
    { "name": "BAR", "position": { "x": 95, "y": 40 } }
  ],
  "zones": [
    {
      "name": "Zone A",
      "color": "#5aa35a",
      "pricing": [
        { "type": "circle", "packagePrice": 2400, "package": "1 TOWER + 1 ICE" },
        { "type": "square", "packagePrice": 4800, "package": "2 TOWER + 2 ICE" }
      ],
      "tables": [
        { "number": "A1", "type": "circle", "position": { "x": 10, "y": 15 } },
        { "number": "A2", "type": "square", "position": { "x": 25, "y": 15 } }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Zone B",
      "color": "#2a7f7f",
      "pricing": [
        { "type": "sofa",     "packagePrice": 6000, "package": "3 TOWER + 3 ICE" },
        { "type": "triangle", "packagePrice": 700,  "package": "1 JUG + 1 ICE" }
      ],
      "tables": [
        { "number": "B1", "type": "sofa", "position": { "x": 75, "y": 30 } },
        { "number": "T1", "type": "triangle", "position": { "x": 90, "y": 30 } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### 4. GET ONE — read back the plan we just created
GET {{host}}/floorplans/{{created.response.body._id}}

### 5. PUT — full replace of the created plan (rename, activate, new layout)
PUT {{host}}/floorplans/{{created.response.body._id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Underground Layout - DJ Night (v2)",
  "venue": "La Loy Bar, Nanglinchee / Rama 3",
  "status": "active",
  "extraPersonFee": 600,
  "landmarks": [
    { "name": "DJ BOOTH", "position": { "x": 50, "y": 5 } },
    { "name": "BAR", "position": { "x": 95, "y": 40 } }
  ],
  "zones": [
    {
      "name": "Zone A",
      "color": "#5aa35a",
      "pricing": [
        { "type": "circle", "packagePrice": 2400, "package": "1 TOWER + 1 ICE" },
        { "type": "square", "packagePrice": 4800, "package": "2 TOWER + 2 ICE" },
        { "type": "sofa",   "packagePrice": 7200, "package": "3 TOWER + 3 ICE" }
      ],
      "tables": [
        { "number": "A1", "type": "circle", "position": { "x": 10, "y": 15 } },
        { "number": "A2", "type": "square", "position": { "x": 25, "y": 15 } },
        { "number": "A3", "type": "sofa",   "position": { "x": 40, "y": 15 } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

### 5b. PATCH — partial update: only change the status of the seeded plan (active -> draft)
PATCH {{host}}/floorplans/{{seededId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "draft"
}

### 6. DELETE — remove the created plan
DELETE {{host}}/floorplans/{{created.response.body._id}}

### 6b. GET ONE after delete — expect 404
GET {{host}}/floorplans/{{created.response.body._id}}

### ---------------------------------------------------------------
### Error cases (status codes)
### ---------------------------------------------------------------

### E1. GET ONE with a malformed id — expect 400
GET {{host}}/floorplans/not-a-valid-id

### E2. GET ONE with a well-formed but unknown id — expect 404
GET {{host}}/floorplans/66f00000000000000000ffff

### E3. POST with missing required fields — expect 400 (validation)
POST {{host}}/floorplans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "zones": []
}

### E4. POST with duplicate table numbers across zones — expect 400 (UC-04 business rule)
POST {{host}}/floorplans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Broken plan",
  "zones": [
    { "name": "Zone A", "pricing": [ { "type": "square", "packagePrice": 4800 } ], "tables": [ { "number": "X1", "type": "square" } ] },
    { "name": "Zone B", "pricing": [ { "type": "circle", "packagePrice": 2000 } ], "tables": [ { "number": "X1", "type": "circle" } ] }
  ]
}

### E5. POST with an invalid table type — expect 400 (enum)
POST {{host}}/floorplans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Wrong type plan",
  "zones": [
    { "name": "Zone A", "pricing": [ { "type": "circle", "packagePrice": 2400 } ], "tables": [ { "number": "Y1", "type": "booth" } ] }
  ]
}

### E6. POST with a table whose type has no price in its zone — expect 400 (pricing rule)
POST {{host}}/floorplans
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Unpriced plan",
  "zones": [
    {
      "name": "Zone A",
      "pricing": [ { "type": "circle", "packagePrice": 2400, "package": "1 TOWER + 1 ICE" } ],
      "tables": [
        { "number": "A1", "type": "circle" },
        { "number": "A2", "type": "sofa" }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
